    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Burning pain in the upper stomach for a week. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sitting Bull came in without an appointment, with the interpreter, because of a burning pain in the upper stomach for a week, worse an hour after meals and at night, six weeks after starting naproxen 500 mg twice daily. He has taken it with food as advised. He has had no vomiting, no black or bloody stools, no trouble swallowing and no weight loss beyond what he intended. He has never had stomach trouble before. Two weeks ago he had the subtalar injection, and his foot is much better. He takes no aspirin, does not drink alcohol and uses no commercial tobacco. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>One week ago, six weeks after starting naproxen</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Upper abdomen, under the breastbone</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>One week</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Burning</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; wakes him some nights</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>After meals and at night</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Naproxen 500 mg twice daily with food for six weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Eating briefly eases it</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No vomiting, black stools, trouble swallowing or weight loss</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

